        {
          "id": "blk_ma13s6qs49",
          "type": "text",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "content": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "In the spring of 2019, eleven farmers met in the back room of the Kingston library to talk about a problem none of them could solve alone. Each had lost a wholesale buyer because they couldn't keep produce cold long enough to deliver it. Together, they could afford a cooler. Within a year they had a cooler, a truck and twenty more members."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The Food Commons is a cooperative: every member owns one share and has one vote. A steering committee of seven, elected each January, runs the day-to-day; big decisions go to the general assembly, which meets four times a year in a different member's barn. Our budget, minutes and bylaws are published for every member to read."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "variant": "drop-cap"
        }
      ]
    },
